# Spec Chum — project rules

- Emulator workspace: `z80`, `bus`, `ula`, `tape`, `formats`, `machine`, `app`.
- Prefer additive changes inside the owning crate; avoid drive-by refactors across crates.
- Never edit plan files under `.cursor/plans/` (or similar).
- Never commit ROM binaries; fetch with `./scripts/fetch_roms.sh`.
- Before finishing Rust work: while iterating prefer `./scripts/check_crates.sh` (debug, scoped crates); before merge run `./scripts/check.sh` (fmt + clippy `-D warnings` + tests). Living room uses `./scripts/check_living_room.sh` (**release** by default — avoid Bevy debug).
- Before tagging a `vX.Y.Z` release: run `./scripts/run_slow_tests.sh` (z80doc + system-tests + z80full) — see `docs/RELEASE.md`. Default CI is not enough.
- Follow `AGENTS.md` and `CONTRIBUTING.md` for TDD and PR expectations.
- Before implementing, check GitHub Issues (`gh issue list` / related `gh issue view`); see `github-issues.mdc`.
- **GUI parity:** egui (`crates/app`) and SpecChumMac (`apps/macos`) stay feature-aligned unless truly platform-specific — see `gui-app-parity.mdc`.
- Before finish/merge of a PR: undraft if needed, run local CR, request GitHub CodeRabbit when quota allows, run `./scripts/check_pr_reviews.sh`. Drafts skip CR completeness; ready PRs hard-fail on pending/missing/error CR or unresolved bot threads; **rate-limited / skipped** soft-passes gate 1 (local CR + threads still required) — see `pr-review-merge.mdc` (lesson #83).
